      "resolved_at": null,
      "message": "@Emily Wachowiak while working on the draft patch https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D222101 (which is meant to make installing a softblocked addon to hit a failure) I've added a placeholder for a new string (and so it is not going to be the generic \"corrupted\" error) and while doing that I noticed that the current message used for the install error on hard-blocked addons is the following:\n\naddon-install-error-blocklisted = { $addonName } could not be installed because it has a high risk of causing stability or security problems.\n\nAnd so in the new placeholder string for the install error on soft-blocked addons I kept the same convetion:\n\naddon-install-error-blocklisted-softblock = { $addonName } could not be installed because it violates Mozilla\u2019s policies.",
      "reactions": [],
