      "created_at": "2024-09-16T21:20:40.163Z",
      "resolved_at": null,
      "message": "@Emily Wachowiak while working on https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D222366 I noticed that the existing hard-block message is including the add-on name (\"{ $name } has been disabled due to security or stability issues.\") and so it felt like we should keep it consistent in the short term (and then eventually consider changing the convention for all the strings used in the same message-bar).\n\nFor that reason the string I've currently included in the draft patch I've linked here (string that I currently consider a placeholder because I wanted to point that out to you before finalizing that patch) follows the same convention:\n\n\"{ $name } violates Mozilla\u2019s policies and has been disabled for your safety. You can re-enable it, but this may be risky.\"",
      "reactions": [],
